mk_txn function:

```
function automatic txn_t mk_txn(input logic [IW-1:0] id, input logic [AW-1:0] addr,
                                input logic [7:0] ulen, input int size);
  txn_t t;
  longint unsigned bb, dsz, first, last;
  bb = 64'd1 << size;
  t.id = id; t.addr = addr; t.size = size; t.ulen = int'(ulen);
  t.sbb = int'(bb);
  t.sal = addr & ~(bb-1);
  t.total = (int'(ulen)+1)*bb - (addr - t.sal);
  t.dsize = (size < 1) ? size : 1;
  dsz = 64'd1 << t.dsize;
  t.dbb = int'(dsz);
  t.dal = addr & ~(dsz-1);
  first = addr;
  last = addr + t.total - 1;
  t.dlen = int'(((last & ~(dsz-1)) - (first & ~(dsz-1))) / dsz);
  return t;
endfunction
```
`addr & ~(bb-1)`: bb is longint unsigned; addr widens. OK. `~(bb-1)` fine.

